# NONSECRET reference only. Do not pass this template as a launch-ready env file.
# Keep real configuration outside the repository; never reuse baseline paths/tags.
# Fill these blank values in the parent shell or a dedicated external runtime file.
LINGUALOOP_ROLES_DB_PASSWORD_FILE=
LINGUALOOP_ROLES_API_IMAGE=
LINGUALOOP_ROLES_WEB_IMAGE=
LINGUALOOP_ROLES_GOOGLE_ENV_FILE=
LINGUALOOP_ROLES_TOKEN_SIGNING_KEY_FILE=

# Dedicated Google env file names below; no example credentials are provided.
# GOOGLE_CLIENT_ID=<real registered client ID>
# GOOGLE_CLIENT_SECRET=<real Google client secret>
# Do NOT set LINGUALOOP_TOKEN_SIGNING_KEY (inline) or auth bypass/identity mocks.
# Compose fixes these application settings; they are not Compose inputs:
# PORT=5000
# LINGUALOOP_DB_HOST=postgres
# LINGUALOOP_DB_PORT=5432
# LINGUALOOP_DB_PASSWORD_FILE=/run/secrets/roles_db_password
# LINGUALOOP_TOKEN_SIGNING_KEY_FILE=/run/secrets/roles_token_signing_key
# GOOGLE_CALLBACK_URL=http://127.0.0.1:5100/auth/google/callback
# LINGUALOOP_WEB_ORIGIN=http://127.0.0.1:5101

# Parent-only setup (not performed by packaging):
# Provision a NEW external directory, e.g. /tmp/lingualoop-roles-t4-private,
# mode 0700, not a baseline secret location. Provision a fresh DB password file
# containing 64 lowercase hex characters (32 random bytes), optional final LF.
# Provision an independent signing key >=32 bytes, regular nonsymlink file,
# owner-readable only (0400 or 0600); Compose bind secrets may retain host mode.
# Provide Google values in a dedicated owner-only env file. Missing real Google
# credentials or the confirmed first-admin email are launch gates, not bypasses.
# Register callback URI http://127.0.0.1:5100/auth/google/callback and browser
# origin http://127.0.0.1:5101 in Google Console. Use verified/confirmed email.
# API/web images must be parent-built from reviewed integrated sources in clean
# isolated context and loaded locally with NEW unique tags, not baseline tags.
# No build context, source mounts, provider keys, model mounts or paid calls here.
# Model-dependent practice paths may remain unavailable; later enable only
# reviewed read-only artifacts/config, with original artifact hashes unchanged.
# Strict real auth must be verified against the integrated image before launch;
# /health alone is NOT proof of configured Google auth or role authorization.

# DB-only configuration (omit app override AND Google/image settings):
# docker compose --env-file /dev/null -f compose.roles-integration.yml config --quiet
# Parent-authorized later start ONLY:
# docker compose --env-file /dev/null -f compose.roles-integration.yml up -d postgres
# TCP target: 127.0.0.1:5543 -> new postgres:5432, database/user lingualoop.
# Before migrations/bootstrap, prove container/network/volume identities differ
# from baseline; then query pg_control_system().system_identifier over TCP to
# the new target and compare with independently obtained baseline identifier.
# Also verify current_database(), current_user, inet_server_addr(),
# inet_server_port(), and empty/new schema. pg_isready is NOT cluster proof.
# API host must remain postgres; roles-db alias is available to offline bootstrap
# tooling only after parent cluster proof. No automatic bootstrap or migrations.
# Real-DB harness may mock dependencies ONLY inside its test module.

# Combined app configuration/start AFTER proof, explicit migrations/bootstrap,
# real auth setup and parent image verification (never combine baseline files):
# docker compose --env-file /dev/null -f compose.roles-integration.yml -f compose.roles-app.yml --profile app config --quiet
# docker compose --env-file /dev/null -f compose.roles-integration.yml -f compose.roles-app.yml --profile app up -d
# UI (all approved roles): http://127.0.0.1:5101/language-practice
# API: http://127.0.0.1:5100 ; browser proxy: http://127.0.0.1:5101/api/
# Admin/teacher/student rights derive from approved accounts, not URL or env flags.
# All starts, TCP checks, migrations/bootstrap, OAuth and HTTP/UI checks remain
# parent-owned and pending. Never print resolved Compose config or secrets.
